            "is_group": false,
            "biography": "Born November 21, 1985 in Mission, British Columbia, Carly Rae Jepsen began performing as a teenager and gained national attention as a contestant on Canadian Idol (2007). After placing on the show she released early, folk-tinged material and steadily built a songwriting career. Her breakout came in 2011 with the single \"Call Me Maybe,\" which became a global phenomenon and led to her major-label debut album Kiss (2012). Jepsen followed mainstream success with a shift toward lush, 1980s-influenced synth-pop on Emotion (2015), an album that earned strong critical praise and a devoted cult following. She has continued releasing pop records, EPs and standalone singles while touring internationally and collaborating with other pop and indie producers.",
            "known_for": "Sharp, hook-driven pop songwriting, infectious melodies, the global hit \"Call Me Maybe\" and the critically acclaimed synth-pop album Emotion.",
            "start_year": 2006,
            "voice_type": [
              "Soprano"
            ],
            "description": "Carly Rae Jepsen is a Canadian singer-songwriter who rose to fame after placing on Canadian Idol and then achieving international success with the 2011 viral hit \"Call Me Maybe.\" Her catalog spans bright mainstream pop, synth-driven indie pop and earlier folk/acoustic work. Widely praised for her craft of concise, hook-forward songwriting, Jepsen balances radio-ready singles with critically acclaimed albums such as Emotion (2015) and Dedicated (2019). She is known for melodic hooks, layered harmonies and emotive lyricism.",
