            "cultural_impact": "Her 2011 single \"Call Me Maybe\" became a viral cultural phenomenon, turning Jepsen into a mainstream pop figure and spawning countless parodies and memes. Later critical reappraisal of Emotion elevated her status as a modern pop craftsman, influencing a wave of synth-forward indie-pop and demonstrating that mainstream hooks can coexist with sophisticated, emotionally literate songwriting. She also maintains a passionate, diverse fanbase including strong support within LGBTQ+ communities.",
